{"v":[[1,"I am come into my garden, my sister, my spouse: I have gathered my myrrh with my spice; I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk: eat, O friends; drink, yea, drink abundantly, O beloved."],[2,"I sleep, but my heart waketh: it is the voice of my beloved that knocketh, saying, Open to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled: for my head is filled with dew, and my locks with the drops of the night."],[3,"I have put off my coat; how shall I put it on? I have washed my feet; how shall I defile them?"],[4,"My beloved put in his hand by the hole of the door, and my bowels were moved for him."],[5,"I rose up to open to my beloved; and my hands dropped with myrrh, and my fingers with sweet smelling myrrh, upon the handles of the lock."],[6,"I opened to my beloved; but my beloved had withdrawn himself, and was gone: my soul failed when he spake: I sought him, but I could not find him; I called him, but he gave me no answer."],[7,"The watchmen that went about the city found me, they smote me, they wounded me; the keepers of the walls took away my veil from me."],[8,"I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, if ye find my beloved, that ye tell him, that I am sick of love."],[9,"What is thy beloved more than another beloved, O thou fairest among women? what is thy beloved more than another beloved, that thou dost so charge us?"],[10,"My beloved is white and ruddy, the chiefest among ten thousand."],[11,"His head is as the most fine gold, his locks are bushy, and black as a raven."],[12,"His eyes are as the eyes of doves by the rivers of waters, washed with milk, and fitly set."],[13,"His cheeks are as a bed of spices, as sweet flowers: his lips like lilies, dropping sweet smelling myrrh."],[14,"His hands are as gold rings set with the beryl: his belly is as bright ivory overlaid with sapphires."],[15,"His legs are as pillars of marble, set upon sockets of fine gold: his countenance is as Lebanon, excellent as the cedars."],[16,"His mouth is most sweet: yea, he is altogether lovely. This is my beloved, and this is my friend, O daughters of Jerusalem."]],"w":{"1":[["bati","I have come","H935"],["le-gan-i","to garden my","H1588"],["'achot-i","O sister my","H269"],["khalah","bride","H3618"],["'ariti","I have gathered","H717"],["mor-i","myrrh my","H4753"],["'im","with","H5973"],["besam-i","spice my","H1313"],["'akhalti","I have eaten","H398"],["ya'r-i","honeycomb my","H3293"],["'im","with","H5973"],["divsh-i","honey my","H1706"],["shatiti","I have drunk","H8354"],["yein-i","wine my","H3196"],["'im","with","H5973"],["chalav-i","milk my","H2461"],["'ikhlu","eat","H398"],["re'im","O friends","H7453"],["shetu","drink","H8354"],["ve-shikhru","and become drunk","H7937"],["dodim","O lovers","H1730"]],"2":[["'ani","I","H589"],["yeshenah","[was] sleeping","H3463"],["ve-lib-i","and heart my","H3820"],["'er","[was] awake","H5782"],["kol","[the] sound of","H6963"],["dod-i","lover my","H1730"],["dofek","knocking","H1849"],["pitchi","open","H6605"],["l-i","to me",""],["'achot-i","O sister my","H269"],["ra'yat-i","friend my","H7474"],["yonat-i","dove my","H3123"],["tamat-i","perfect [one] my","H8535"],["she-rosh-i","that head my","H7218"],["nimla'","[is] filled","H4390"],["tal","dew","H2919"],["kevutzota-i","locks my","H6977"],["resisei","dewdrops of","H7447"],["layelah","night","H3915"]],"3":[["pashati","I have taken off","H6584"],["'et","<obj.>","H853"],["kutanet-i","tunic my","H3801"],["'eikhakhah","how?","H349"],["'elbashe-nah","will I put on it","H3847"],["rachatzti","I have washed","H7364"],["'et","<obj.>","H853"],["ragla-i","feet my","H7272"],["'eikhakhah","how?","H349"],["'atanefe-m","will I dirty them","H2936"]],"4":[["dod-i","lover my","H1730"],["shalach","he sent","H7971"],["yad-o","hand his","H3027"],["min","from","H4480"],["ha-chor","the hole","H2356"],["u-me'a-i","and inward parts my","H4578"],["hamu","they were turbulent","H1993"],["'ala-v","on him","H5921"]],"5":[["kamti","I arose","H6965"],["'an